{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin", "label": "ADR-018 three.js digital twin and the Horizon visual language", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-018-three-js-digital-twin.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_three_js_stack", "label": "three.js + react-three-fiber + drei renderer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-018-three-js-digital-twin.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "three 0.187.0, @react-three/fiber 9.8.2, @react-three/drei 10.7.9, all MIT browser libraries with no network access so the air-gap profile is unaffected; bundled, never fetched. Chosen after Syed's customer judged the console generic and asked for a real 3D twin instead of isometric SVG."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_twinscene", "label": "TwinScene.tsx (client-only chunk)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-018-three-js-digital-twin.md", "source_location": "apps/console/src/components/twin/TwinScene.tsx", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Loaded after the page paints via next/dynamic ssr:false so the twin route's first paint is the shell and KPIs and the Lighthouse budget holds."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_twin_model", "label": "twin-model.ts (pure geometry model)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-018-three-js-digital-twin.md", "source_location": "apps/console/src/lib/twin-model.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Racks query becomes rooms tiled in a grid, racks placed by row/position at true proportions (0.6 m x 1.2 m, 44.45 mm per U), device plates stacked in layer colour; impact graph lifted onto stacked planes in CI_LAYERS order. Pure and unit tested so the scene only draws."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_instancing_on_demand", "label": "Instanced meshes and on-demand rendering", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-018-three-js-digital-twin.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Racks, devices and nodes are instanced meshes (one draw call per kind), edges are Line2 segments, rendering is on demand so an idle twin costs no frames; this is how 60 fps holds on a 100k-CI estate."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_twin_constants", "label": "TWIN constants in @openmap/constants", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-018-three-js-digital-twin.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every dimension, threshold, camera and lighting number lives here with a rationale so apps/console carries no numeric literal (guard rule)."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_sigma_2d_map", "label": "Sigma.js 2D dependency map (ADR-007)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-018-three-js-digital-twin.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Remains the 2D dependency map; the twin is a second view over the same impact result, not a replacement."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_horizon_visual_language", "label": "Horizon visual language", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-018-three-js-digital-twin.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A distinctive surface language delivered through tokens, unlayered rules and four shared components so every existing screen inherited it without per-screen edits; Lighthouse accessibility stays at 1.0 because contrast tokens are unchanged."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_effects_tokens", "label": "packages/ui/src/tokens/effects.ts", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-018-three-js-digital-twin.md", "source_location": "packages/ui/src/tokens/effects.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_chakra_petch_display_face", "label": "Chakra Petch display face", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-018-three-js-digital-twin.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_obsidian_pro", "label": "Obsidian Pro direction", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-018-three-js-digital-twin.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_req_ui_028", "label": "REQ-UI-028", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-018-three-js-digital-twin.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_req_ui_029", "label": "REQ-UI-029", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-018-three-js-digital-twin.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin", "target": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_three_js_stack", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-018-three-js-digital-twin.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_twinscene", "target": "docs_adr_adr_018_three_js_digital_twin_three_js_stack", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/AD